wireview-hwmon (1.5.0~26.04.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * wireviewd: serial handover protocol (suspend/resume serial) so clients
    like the WireView Linux app can borrow the USB serial port for device
    log reads, theme uploads, and firmware flashing while the daemon pauses
    polling; relayed commands are logged and rejected while suspended.
  * wireviewctl: new "flash" command - update the device firmware over DFU
    via dfu-util, enters the bootloader through the daemon when needed and
    works headless with -y.
  * Ship the official firmware image (v05) at
    /usr/share/wireview/TG-WV-PRO2-FW.hex; "wireviewctl flash" with no file
    argument uses it, so "wireviewctl flash -y" is a complete update.
  * Recommend dfu-util (used by the flash command).

 -- Emanuele Sparvoli <sparvoli@gmail.com>  Fri, 10 Jul 2026 10:40:00 +0000

